# Ownership is team based so review never depends on one person being available.
# Every path has an owner. A path with no owner is a coverage gap, not a silence.
#
# GitHub silently ignores an entry naming a team it cannot resolve, which turns this
# file into an inert required check. A team resolves only inside the organization that
# owns the repository, so a slug from a sibling organization is ignored exactly like a
# slug that does not exist. This repository is EtharaOrion/trinity, so every slug below
# names an EtharaOrion team and each one is verified to exist there; the parallel teams
# in Ethara-Ai govern that organization's repositories and are never owners here. When a
# specialised team is created, change only the owner column of the rows it should hold;
# the path structure already separates contracts, harness, supply chain, and research so
# that split is a one line edit.

* @EtharaOrion/research

# The four contract documents are the product. A change here changes the
# obligations of every project that vendors Trinity.

/ENGRAM.md   @EtharaOrion/trinity
/FORGE.md    @EtharaOrion/trinity
/CRUCIBLE.md @EtharaOrion/trinity
/README.md   @EtharaOrion/trinity

# Attachments are subordinate to the contracts but still bind implementation.

/specifications/ @EtharaOrion/trinity

# The gate. A weakened rule here lets a downstream project pass an audit it
# should fail, which is the primary threat named in SECURITY.md.

/tools/ @EtharaOrion/trinity
/tests/ @EtharaOrion/trinity

# Supply chain surface. Action pins and dependency declarations.

/.github/         @EtharaOrion/trinity
/pyproject.toml   @EtharaOrion/trinity
/uv.lock          @EtharaOrion/trinity
/.python-version  @EtharaOrion/trinity

# The shared research corpus is ENGRAM owned by contract.

/research/ @EtharaOrion/trinity
